#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: onColor()"
msgstr "# Fungsi: onColor()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* `surface`. This is the CSS-only\nform of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand button, a\nprimary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a fixed inverse token,\nit picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the surface changes."
msgstr "Foreground yang mudah dibaca — hitam atau putih — untuk kandungan yang diletakkan *pada* `surface`. Ini ialah bentuk hanya-CSS bagi varian `*-on-color` InstUI yang berulang (cincin fokus pada butang jenama, teks butang primary-inverse, ikon pada permukaan berwarna): bukannya token inverse tetap, ia memilih kontras dari permukaan itu sendiri, jadi ia kekal betul apabila permukaan berubah."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and snaps it to `0` (black) or\n`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no JS, no fixed hex."
msgstr "Ia membaca kecerahan OKLCH permukaan melalui sintaks warna relatif dan menentukannya kepada `0` (hitam) atau\n`1` (putih) pada `threshold` menggunakan helah clamp `calc(… * infinity)` — tiada JS, tiada hex tetap."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### surface"
msgstr "### surface"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
