#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# colors"
msgstr "# colors"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — matematik warna hanya CSS yang mencerminkan pembantu InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\npembantu (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."
msgstr "InstUI mengira itu pada masa bina dengan `tinycolor2` terhadap nilai hex konkrit. pantoken mengeluarkan\nrujukan `var(--instui-*)` yang diselesaikan dalam penyemak imbas (sering melalui `light-dark()`), jadi\npengiraan perlu berlaku dalam CSS sebaliknya. Setiap pembantu mengembalikan rentetan warna CSS yang dibina daripada\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) dan\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nkedua-duanya ciri asas penyemak imbas moden — jadi satu ungkapan menjejak token walaupun ia sepasang\n`light-dark()` bergantung pada skim. Gunakannya di mana sahaja anda sebaliknya akan mengekod keras warna terbitan."

